invariant: INV-17
file: src/aead_avx512.c
catches: test/avx512-run.sh bin/aead_avx512_equiv_test
builds: bin/aead_avx512_equiv_test
reason: aead_avx512_seal returns without wiping its input words, eight of them
  the key, so its dead frame keeps the key side by side. Every tag is
  still right. bin/aead_avx512_equiv_test copies the stack below a seal
  and looks for the key. It needs a CPU with AVX-512 IFMA, or Intel SDE
  through SDE64, which the nightly's test-invariants job installs; without
  either this reports unguarded rather than caught.

--- old
    ct_wipe(words, sizeof words);
    hash_rest(p, h, &of_r, ct + hashed, n - hashed);
--- new
    hash_rest(p, h, &of_r, ct + hashed, n - hashed);
